<exercise xml:id="practice-volumes-1">
  <title>Rotation About the \(x\)-Axis</title>

  <statement>
    <p>
      Find the volume of the solid obtained by rotating the region bounded
      by
      <m>y=x^3+2</m>,
      <m>x=0</m>,
      and
      <m>x=1</m>
      about the <m>x</m>-axis.
    </p>
  </statement>

  <solution>
    <p>
      Using the disk method, the volume is
    </p>

    <me>
      V
      =
      \pi\int_0^1 (x^3+2)^2\,dx.
    </me>

    <p>
      Expanding the integrand,
    </p>

    <me>
      V
      =
      \pi\int_0^1
      \left(x^6+4x^3+4\right)\,dx.
    </me>

    <p>
      Therefore,
    </p>

    <me>
      V
      =
      \pi
      \left[
        \frac{x^7}{7}
        +x^4
        +4x
      \right]_0^1
      =
      \frac{36\pi}{7}.
    </me>

    <p>
      Thus, the volume is
      <m>\frac{36\pi}{7}</m> cubic units.
    </p>
  </solution>
</exercise>